Package: immunread
Title: Convenient Parsers for Popular Immune Repertoire Data Formats
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Vadim I.", "Nazarov", , "support@immunomind.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3659-2709"))
Contact: support@immunomind.com
Description: Provides parser functions for importing adaptive immune receptor
    repertoire (AIRR) data into objects provided by 'immundata'.
    Parsers support the AIRR Community Rearrangement format and outputs from
    'MiXCR', 10x Genomics, BD Genomics, Adaptive Biotechnologies, 'Dandelion',
    'Immcantation', Parse Biosciences, 'TRUST4', and 'WAT3R'.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://immunomind.github.io/docs/, https://github.com/immunomind/immunread
BugReports: https://github.com/immunomind/immunread/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0),
    immundata (>= 0.1.0)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    duckplyr (>= 1.2.1),
    rlang
Suggests: 
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    readr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/testthat/parallel: true
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
Config/Needs/website: altdoc
